Same query, no filter
  -0.000  qbr-2024-Q4.md       Meridian Supply Co. — Quarterly Busi
  -0.000  qbr-2025-Q2.md       Meridian Supply Co. — Quarterly Busi
  -0.000  qbr-2025-Q4.md       Meridian Supply Co. — Quarterly Busi
  Three different quarters, all at distance zero. Every quarterly review opens
  with the same title block, so those chunks are byte-identical and therefore
  have identical vectors. Without the filter there is no way to prefer one.
  This is why Chapter 10 insisted that a chunk carry what it is about, and it
  is the near-duplicate problem Chapter 14 has to solve properly.

After upsert, the text starts: 'REVISED: # Meridian Supply Co. — Quarter'
…and the vector is the OLD one, because we upserted text without re-embedding.
Nothing errored. The document now says one thing and is findable as another.

Every vector store has this failure. Store the hash of the text alongside the
vector, and refuse to serve a chunk whose text no longer matches it.
